Chapter 8

Collective Qualia Posterior under Exchangeability

When multiple agents each provide a subjective report about the same world state, their reports are rarely conditionally independent given the world. Cultural, linguistic, and contextual factors introduce correlation. We replace the false independence assumption with the weaker condition of exchangeability.

Definition 8.1 (Collective Posterior under de Finetti Exchangeability).
Assume the sequence of reports  R_1, \dots, R_N  is exchangeable. By de Finetti’s theorem, there exists a latent random measure  \Theta  on the space of report-generating distributions such that, conditional on  \Theta , the reports are i.i.d. Hence,

P(R_{1:N} \mid W = w) = \int_{\Theta} \prod_{i=1}^N \left( \int_{\mathcal{E}} P(R_i \mid E, \Theta) \, P(E \mid w) \, \mathrm{d}E \right) \mathrm{d}\mu(\Theta \mid w),
\tag{17}

where  \mu(\Theta \mid w)  is a prior over the shared latent factor.

The augmented collective posterior is then

P(w \mid R_{1:N}, O) \propto P(O \mid w) \,
\Bigg[ \int_{\Theta} \prod_{i=1}^N \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_Q(R_i; w, \Theta) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(\Theta \mid w) \Bigg] \, \mu_W(w),
\tag{18}

with  \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_Q(R_i; w, \Theta) = \int_{\mathcal{E}} P(R_i \mid E, \Theta) \, P(E \mid w) \, \mathrm{d}E .

The difference between this corrected posterior and the naive product-of-likelihoods formula (which assumes conditional independence) can be bounded. Let  \operatorname{MI}(R_i; R_j \mid W)  denote the residual mutual information between two reports given the world state. Then

\bigl| \log P_{\text{naive}}(w \mid R_{1:N}, O) - \log P_{\text{corrected}}(w \mid R_{1:N}, O) \bigr|
\le \sum_{1 \le i < j \le N} \operatorname{MI}(R_i; R_j \mid W=w) + O(1).

If the pairwise mutual information is small, the simple product is adequate; otherwise, the hierarchical model with latent  \Theta  must be used to avoid double-counting correlated evidence.

