Appendix F

Jensen Gap and Pinsker’s Inequality

F.1. Statement of Pinsker’s Inequality

For any two probability measures P and Q on the same measurable space,

\|P - Q\|_{\mathrm{TV}} \le \sqrt{\frac{1}{2} D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P \,\|\, Q)}.

F.2. Application to the ELBO Gap

The gap is \Delta = D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q_\phi(E \mid R) \,\|\, P(E \mid R, W)). Hence,

\| q_\phi - P(\cdot \mid R, W) \|_{\mathrm{TV}} \le \sqrt{\frac{\Delta}{2}}.

A gap of \Delta < 0.01 nats guarantees a total variation distance less than 0.071, meaning the variational posterior is virtually indistinguishable from the true posterior in any statistical test based on the likelihood.

