Appendix G

Computational Complexity Analysis

G.1. Training Complexity

Let L be the sequence length, d the model dimension, and B the batch size. The forward pass of the world encoder is \mathcal{O}(B L d^2 + B L^2 d). The qualia encoder and decoder add a similar cost for the report sequence length L_R, which is typically much smaller than L. Overall, the RQA overhead is approximately 15\% in wall-clock time relative to a standard language model of equal size.

G.2. Reflective Loop Complexity

At inference, each iteration of the reflective loop requires M evaluations of the qualia likelihood ELBO. With M=100 particles and 5–10 loop iterations, the cost is equivalent to about 500–1000 forward passes of the encoder, which is acceptable for offline or interactive applications where latency is not critical. Caching the prior P_\theta(E \mid O) reduces the per-particle cost to a simple dot product in the embedding space, enabling real-time operation on modern hardware.

