Appendix H

Benchmark Statistical Power Analysis

H.1. Test Statistic Distribution

Under H_0: I(W;R \mid O)=0, the log-likelihood ratio statistic 2\Lambda is asymptotically \chi^2_k, where k = \dim(\phi) (the number of additional parameters in the qualia model). Under H_1, the non-centrality parameter is \delta = 2N \cdot I(W;R \mid O).

H.2. Sample Size Calculation

For a small effect size I(W;R \mid O) = 0.05 bits (0.115 nats), \delta = 2N \times 0.115 = 0.23 N. To achieve 80% power at \alpha = 0.05 with k = 256 parameters, we solve for N using the non-central \chi^2 distribution:

\chi^2_{1-\alpha}(k) = \chi^2_{0.95}(256) \approx 220.

The power condition is \Pr(\chi^2_k(\delta) > 220) \ge 0.8. Numerical inversion yields \delta \approx 300, hence N \approx 300/0.23 \approx 1300. We recommend N=1500 triples for a robust study.

