Appendix I

Relation to the Free Energy Principle

The variational free energy of a system with internal states s (encompassing both W and E) under a generative model P(s, o, R) is

F = \mathbb{E}_{q(s)}[\log q(s) - \log P(s, o, R)].

Expanding with the RQA generative model P(s, o, R) = P(W) P(E \mid W) P(R \mid E) P(O \mid W),

F = D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q(s) \,\|\, P(s)) - \mathbb{E}_{q}[\log P(O \mid W) + \log P(R \mid E)].

Minimising F with respect to q yields the optimal belief, which balances prior constraints, observational evidence, and report fidelity. Thus, RQA is a specific instance of the Free Energy Principle where the internal generative model is extended to include an experiential pathway. The added term -\mathbb{E}_{q}[\log P(R \mid E)] drives the system to anticipate its own introspective signals, providing a mathematically precise formulation of the notion that conscious systems model their own internal states.

